SYNTHESIS
========================================================================================
H has two loneliness readings.
  Low H, especially H=1, detects unanchored bunching: a huge empty semicircle.
  High H detects LRC-style even separation: many vertices have two safe gaps.
Plain H is therefore not the LRC invariant by itself; LRC needs a marked
tournament structure: circular order, stationary vertex, safe-gap mask, and
pressure/deletion data.  H is the scalar shadow of that richer tournament movie.
